{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#ims","id":"hiecm.glossary.ims","summary":"The umbrella term for the software a health facility runs, whichever of HMIS, EMR, LIMS or PMS it happens to be.","title":"IMS, information management system","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#hmis","id":"hiecm.glossary.hmis","summary":"The day to day software of a hospital, under any of its three names. A hospital uses it both to publish its own records and to fetch a patient's history from...","title":"HMIS, HIS or HIMS, the software a hospital runs","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#emr","id":"hiecm.glossary.emr","summary":"The system a hospital or clinic records consultations, prescriptions and results in. A facility uses it both to publish its own records and to fetch a patien...","title":"EMR, the clinical system a provider runs, also written EHR","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#lims","id":"hiecm.glossary.lims","summary":"The system a diagnostic laboratory uses to manage samples, tests and results.","title":"LIMS, laboratory information management system, also written LMIS","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/how-it-fits#roles","id":"hiecm.concept.roles","summary":"Your role, IMS or PHR, is fixed by the entity your software acts for, while HIP and HIU change with the direction each record moves.","title":"Roles, which entity your software acts for and which way the record moves","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#hrp","id":"hiecm.glossary.hrp","summary":"Whoever holds the records. It describes custody, which is why it is neither a position nor a direction.","title":"HRP, health repository provider","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#fhir","id":"shared.glossary.nrces","summary":"The body that publishes the Indian FHIR profiles every ABDM health record must validate against.","title":"NRCeS, National Resource Centre for EHR Standards","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/reference/fhir/codes-and-value-sets#supporting-info-categories","id":"shared.glossary.dsc","summary":"The company that builds ABDM compliant software for patients or health facilities. It is the entity that certifies, as distinct from the software that integr...","title":"DSC, Digital Solution Company","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/reference/fhir/claim-request","id":"nhcx.fhir.claim-request","summary":"The bundle a hospital sends after discharge to claim payment, with the final amounts, the discharge details and the documents the policy requires.","title":"Claim request bundle","type":"fhir"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/milestones/m4#m4-link-bridge","id":"hiecm.flow.m4-link-bridge","summary":"Connect an onboarded facility to the software that will act for it, say whether the facility publishes records through it, fetches them, or both, and name it...","title":"Link a facility to its bridge","type":"flow"}]}
